@@ -130,6 +130,8 @@ pi skills remove browser-testing-with-devtools --repo
 
 `--session` is interactive-only and lasts until the session ends. `--global` and `--repo` persist to their respective JSON configuration. `list` and `search` show catalog skills. `pi skills active` shows the configured global and repository entries; `/skills active` also shows session entries.
 
+Path arguments may use `~`, `$NAME`, or `${NAME}`; `/skills` expands them itself because its arguments never pass through a shell. For the one-shot CLI, quote variable-based paths so the shell passes their spelling unchanged, for example `pi skills add '$SKILL_ROOT/review' --global`. With `--repo`, a path inside the current checkout is stored relative to the repository root, so the entry works in trusted clones and worktrees with the same remote. Checkout-relative entries are activated only after the current checkout is trusted. Otherwise `add` keeps a `~` or `$NAME` spelling as typed and stores any other path as an absolute path, under `~` when it is in your home directory. Stored paths are expanded whenever Pi loads skills: at startup, after `/skills add` or `/skills remove`, and on `/reload` or `/skills reload`. Other relative entries resolve against the repository root in `repo-skills.json` and against the working directory in `skills.json`, so prefer absolute, `~`, or `$NAME` paths in `skills.json`.
+
 Use `--no-skills` to suppress global and repository active skills; explicit `--skill` paths still load.
 
 ## Write portable frontmatter
